WEBVTT

00:01.850 --> 00:03.020
Hello!

00:03.020 --> 00:03.970
What's this?

00:04.220 --> 00:06.080
Come on in, you two!

00:06.080 --> 00:07.090
Thank you.

00:08.810 --> 00:11.120
Why'd the lady saint come, too?

00:11.640 --> 00:14.480
Eric is asking a question, that's all!

00:14.480 --> 00:17.320
Don't say rude things.

00:17.320 --> 00:21.520
But it's only the pastor 
that we've asked to tutor me.

00:18.760 --> 00:19.690
You little...

00:21.520 --> 00:24.200
There's nothing for the lady saint to do.

00:24.200 --> 00:27.170
She said that if I was coming, 
she'd come along, too.

00:27.170 --> 00:29.630
I'll make sure I'm not in the way!

00:29.630 --> 00:32.150
Well, it's not like I mind or anything.

00:32.150 --> 00:35.180
You two just devote yourselves to studying.

00:35.180 --> 00:37.760
The lady saint will stay here 
in the shop with me.

00:37.760 --> 00:39.010
Won't you?

00:39.010 --> 00:40.560
O-Okay!

00:40.560 --> 00:43.770
Please don't use the lady saint 
to attract customers.

00:43.770 --> 00:45.160
Goodness.

00:45.160 --> 00:49.280
I can't help it if customers 
start showing up, can I?

00:53.440 --> 00:55.650
I'm sorry about my mother.

00:56.040 --> 00:59.370
By now, she's probably making 
the lady saint do all sorts of things.

00:59.370 --> 01:02.280
Since it's Miss Rebecca, 
I'm sure the lady saint will be all right.

01:02.280 --> 01:03.660
Are you sure?

01:03.660 --> 01:06.240
I feel like she'll be turned 
into a dress-up doll.

01:06.240 --> 01:08.290
You have a point.

01:10.300 --> 01:14.330
I don't really understand 
what a lady saint is.

01:14.330 --> 01:18.430
What kind of person is 
that lady saint to you, pastor?

01:18.430 --> 01:20.680
What kind?

01:21.640 --> 01:25.370
<i>She's someone I want to make happy, 
someone I want to protect,</i>

01:25.370 --> 01:26.520
<i>and...</i>

01:28.470 --> 01:29.690
Pastor?

01:30.550 --> 01:32.800
Um, well...

01:34.380 --> 01:36.820
I'm not really sure.

01:37.200 --> 01:39.090
Even when we went to the town to the west,

01:39.090 --> 01:43.120
I wasn't sure how to introduce her.

01:43.120 --> 01:46.000
Saying she's a roommate 
seemed too simple, but...

01:47.360 --> 01:49.880
Wouldn't the word be "family"?

01:50.080 --> 01:51.580
Family?

01:51.580 --> 01:54.940
The lady saint seems really happy 
when she's with you, Pastor,

01:54.940 --> 01:59.020
and you're always concerned 
for her well-being.

01:59.400 --> 02:00.470
So...

02:00.470 --> 02:03.200
I thought that's what we 
call "family," isn't it?

02:03.200 --> 02:04.640
Family...

03:36.270 --> 03:39.990
Episode 12

03:36.270 --> 03:39.990
The Shape of Their Relationship

03:40.810 --> 03:43.000
Shall we take a little break?

03:43.320 --> 03:46.040
I'll go see how the lady saint is doing.

03:46.040 --> 03:47.880
I'll go, too.

03:50.520 --> 03:52.060
<i>Family.</i>

03:52.060 --> 03:53.830
<i>Family?</i>

03:54.250 --> 03:57.120
<i>Grandpa, who brought me up, was family.</i>

03:57.680 --> 04:00.880
<i>But the lady saint and I aren't family.</i>

04:01.410 --> 04:04.750
<i>What makes a family?</i>

04:05.520 --> 04:08.510
Oh, how adorable! 
Both of them look lovely. What about...

04:09.140 --> 04:11.910
She really is surrounded by a crowd.

04:12.640 --> 04:14.150
Lawren!

04:14.150 --> 04:15.070
Pastor!

04:15.070 --> 04:17.830
Which dress do you think suits 
the lady saint best?

04:17.830 --> 04:18.650
What?

04:19.220 --> 04:21.570
I think this one's better. 
What do you think?

04:19.230 --> 04:21.580
Even if you ask me, I don't...

04:21.570 --> 04:22.760
Come on.

04:21.570 --> 04:24.580
This one's nice, too, isn't it?

04:22.760 --> 04:26.320
You ran away last time, 
so you need to face it properly this time.

04:30.410 --> 04:33.580
The lady saint looks good in anything.

04:33.580 --> 04:36.360
You just don't understand, do you?

04:36.360 --> 04:39.080
It isn't good to demand too much of him.

04:39.840 --> 04:42.590
It will put Lawren in quite the pickle.

04:44.480 --> 04:45.790
<i>If we were family,</i>

04:45.790 --> 04:48.600
<i>would I be able to say this 
kind of thing, like it was normal?</i>

04:50.600 --> 04:52.990
M-Miss Mell! I didn't know you were here!

04:52.990 --> 04:54.640
Yup, I was here.

04:57.230 --> 04:59.240
Wh-What is it?

04:59.240 --> 05:01.860
I thought maybe you might 
be worrying about something.

05:02.270 --> 05:03.860
Want to talk about it?

05:06.760 --> 05:09.780
Hmm, family, huh?

05:09.780 --> 05:12.280
Wh-Why are you looking at me like that?

05:12.280 --> 05:16.010
Well, it's just that family 
comes in lots of different shapes.

05:16.010 --> 05:18.450
In a way, the word 
fits your situation perfectly.

05:18.450 --> 05:19.880
That's Eric for you.

05:19.880 --> 05:22.290
Well, yes.

05:22.290 --> 05:26.040
I know that there are, of course, 
many kinds of families in the world.

05:26.320 --> 05:27.790
But... How do I put this?

05:27.790 --> 05:31.880
In my case, I feel like it's 
disrespectful to the lady saint.

05:31.880 --> 05:34.430
In a certain sense, yeah, it is rude of you.

05:35.460 --> 05:37.020
In a certain sense?

05:37.020 --> 05:40.120
What meaning does her presence hold for you?

05:40.120 --> 05:42.700
In the end, you decide 
and assign that meaning yourself.

05:42.960 --> 05:44.060
In your case,

05:44.060 --> 05:46.780
the fact that you're thinking 
about it is a huge step forward.

05:46.790 --> 05:47.900
What?

05:47.900 --> 05:49.660
Even though you're a pastor.

05:49.660 --> 05:52.750
I'm sorry, asking you for advice like this.

05:52.750 --> 05:54.580
I don't know what to do 
when it comes to my own issues.

05:54.580 --> 05:56.450
That being so...

05:56.960 --> 06:00.670
there's someone who's been emitting 
an alarming aura for a while now.

06:01.710 --> 06:03.570
Lady Saint!

06:03.570 --> 06:05.220
Please, you should have said something!

06:05.220 --> 06:09.720
L-Lawren, you and the fortune 
teller seem very friendly.

06:09.720 --> 06:12.450
Huh? We're not particularly friendly.

06:12.450 --> 06:15.640
The pastor is pretty cold to me 
from time to time.

06:15.640 --> 06:18.160
Pastor, we should get started again.

06:18.160 --> 06:20.360
Oh, that's right! I'm sorry.

06:20.360 --> 06:23.730
M-May I watch as you help him study?

06:23.730 --> 06:26.280
I won't be any trouble!

06:26.280 --> 06:29.370
If you're quiet, then I don't mind.

06:29.370 --> 06:31.660
Thank you so much, Eric!

06:31.660 --> 06:33.560
Then, I guess I'll get going now.

06:33.560 --> 06:35.450
Thank you, Miss Mell.

06:36.280 --> 06:37.440
Miss Fortune Teller!

06:37.440 --> 06:39.800
We should have a nice 
long chat sometime soo—

06:40.420 --> 06:42.220
Oh! Lady Saint!

06:42.220 --> 06:44.290
I-I'm sorry.

06:44.290 --> 06:48.510
I can help support you 
when I'm nearby, so that's fine, but...

06:53.570 --> 06:55.690
What is it?

06:55.690 --> 06:57.020
Nothing.

06:57.460 --> 07:00.010
Um, Lady Saint?

07:02.480 --> 07:05.140
Pastor, thank you.

07:05.140 --> 07:07.600
Make sure you review what we did today.

07:07.600 --> 07:08.440
I will.

07:08.440 --> 07:10.080
Oh, that's right!

07:10.080 --> 07:12.160
I'm going to have a shop 
in the Winter Market.

07:12.160 --> 07:14.470
I hope you'll both come.

07:14.470 --> 07:16.830
Winter Market?

07:16.830 --> 07:19.750
Oh, it's the first one for you, 
isn't it, Lady Saint?

07:19.750 --> 07:22.620
It's a festival held in various locations.

07:22.620 --> 07:26.800
Lots of different shops set up 
in the square and everyone comes.

07:26.800 --> 07:29.120
It's quite merry and lively.

07:30.640 --> 07:33.400
Everyone builds a big tower together.

07:34.130 --> 07:35.460
I want to go!

07:35.460 --> 07:38.190
Lawren, let's go with Abel and Hazelita!

07:38.190 --> 07:39.050
Yes.

07:39.310 --> 07:40.840
We'll be waiting!

07:43.720 --> 07:45.440
Hey, let go.

07:49.690 --> 07:53.210
I'm looking forward to the Winter Market!

07:53.210 --> 07:56.310
Oh, I'd like to help 
with the preparations, too!

07:57.000 --> 07:59.200
Um, Lady Saint?

08:00.460 --> 08:04.590
Lady Saint, what do you think a family is?

08:04.590 --> 08:06.360
Family?

08:06.840 --> 08:08.970
Why are you asking that all of a sudden?

08:08.970 --> 08:12.660
I was thinking that Eric's 
home life is nice, that's all.

08:13.960 --> 08:18.090
I think Eric's home is lovely, too.

08:18.090 --> 08:20.200
Let's see.

08:21.410 --> 08:23.600
You eat meals together,

08:24.000 --> 08:26.610
you say "good night" before you sleep,

08:26.610 --> 08:29.760
and they're the first ones you 
say "hello" to in the morning.

08:29.760 --> 08:30.980
That's your family.

08:30.980 --> 08:33.610
That's what I think, anyway.

08:36.610 --> 08:39.540
Oh, but that's just my opinion.

08:41.270 --> 08:44.720
I might have been making it 
a little too complicated.

08:45.680 --> 08:48.910
Lady Saint, you've given me 
an answer that's easily understood.

08:49.830 --> 08:51.880
Well, I am a lady saint, after all!

08:53.760 --> 08:56.030
All right, that's good. 
Now, go slowly there.

08:56.030 --> 08:57.270
Come on. That's right!

08:57.280 --> 08:59.310
You're very good at this!

08:59.310 --> 09:02.650
It's so pretty! 
What if we added flowers there?

09:01.700 --> 09:03.970
So, that's what happened.

09:02.650 --> 09:03.970
That would be lovely! Yes!

09:05.720 --> 09:09.480
Apparently, the lady saint 
and I are like family.

09:11.600 --> 09:14.880
What are you saying?

09:14.880 --> 09:15.720
What?

09:15.720 --> 09:19.020
It's the long way around, 
but that fine, isn't it?

09:19.020 --> 09:21.800
There's no need to unleash 
your bloodlust like that, miss.

09:21.800 --> 09:24.120
Abel, you are much too 
lenient with Lawrence!

09:24.120 --> 09:25.610
He's my friend.

09:25.610 --> 09:27.920
And I already know he's dense.

09:27.920 --> 09:28.610
Besides,

09:28.610 --> 09:33.600
acknowledging her as family means 
he's not taking her for granted, right?

09:34.700 --> 09:36.660
Well, if you're going to go 
that far with it.

09:36.660 --> 09:39.520
If you don't show that 
you're family in some way,

09:39.520 --> 09:41.620
I'll feel bad for Cecilia.

09:41.620 --> 09:43.600
Sh-Show we're family?

09:43.840 --> 09:45.840
How?

09:45.840 --> 09:46.850
Uh...

09:51.470 --> 09:53.040
What?!

09:54.940 --> 09:57.950
I'll wear this when we go.

09:59.450 --> 10:01.950
Defense against the cold

10:00.550 --> 10:01.950
Glare.

10:04.090 --> 10:06.580
Lawren! Hurry! Hurry!

10:06.580 --> 10:09.580
Lady Saint, please don't run!

10:18.080 --> 10:20.630
Lawren, it's the tower 
everyone built together!

10:20.630 --> 10:21.480
It's so impressive!

10:21.480 --> 10:22.490
Yes.

10:22.490 --> 10:24.330
Where shall we start looking around?

10:24.330 --> 10:26.970
Cecilia, what do you want to see?

10:26.970 --> 10:27.750
Everything!

10:27.750 --> 10:29.010
Everything, huh?

10:29.010 --> 10:31.440
We have to hurry up 
or we won't get to everything!

10:31.440 --> 10:33.480
Now, let's go!

10:33.480 --> 10:36.410
Lady Saint! Wait, please!

10:36.410 --> 10:38.330
Come on, we're going.

10:38.330 --> 10:39.810
Yes, yes.

11:12.730 --> 11:16.060
I wonder where Abel and Hazelita have gone.

11:16.060 --> 11:17.920
We've gotten separated from them.

11:17.920 --> 11:21.030
Lady Saint! Pastor!

11:22.440 --> 11:23.680
Lily!

11:23.680 --> 11:24.820
Hello.

11:24.820 --> 11:27.950
You're really cute today, Lady Saint!

11:27.950 --> 11:28.790
What?

11:28.790 --> 11:30.880
I-I'm not really...

11:33.790 --> 11:35.420
I thought so.

11:35.420 --> 11:36.360
What?

11:36.360 --> 11:37.840
Bye, then!

11:40.880 --> 11:42.280
Pastor!

11:43.400 --> 11:44.490
Oh!

11:44.490 --> 11:46.180
Come and stop by for a while!

11:46.180 --> 11:48.440
Oh, this is where you were!

11:48.440 --> 11:49.380
That's right.

11:49.380 --> 11:53.120
Pastor, would you lend me the lady saint 
to draw in some customers?

11:53.120 --> 11:53.880
What?

11:53.880 --> 11:55.430
I'm not lending her out.

11:56.190 --> 11:56.950
Just kidding.

11:56.950 --> 11:59.360
I'm doing very well today.

11:59.360 --> 12:00.770
I'm taking a break right now.

12:00.770 --> 12:02.750
I see.

12:02.750 --> 12:04.210
Lady Saint.

12:04.950 --> 12:06.310
Come here for a minute.

12:07.110 --> 12:10.450
This is a new piece I've just finished.

12:10.450 --> 12:12.800
Oh, it's lovely!

12:12.800 --> 12:15.600
What do you think of it 
for the lady saint, pastor?

12:16.680 --> 12:19.360
I-I think it would look very nice on her.

12:22.690 --> 12:25.340
Why do you hit me like that?

12:25.840 --> 12:27.840
Lady Saint...

12:28.960 --> 12:31.720
Pastor, could it be that you—

12:31.720 --> 12:34.850
That's something which shouldn't be said.

12:36.060 --> 12:37.600
Why not?

12:37.600 --> 12:39.400
Everyone knows, don't they?

12:39.400 --> 12:41.360
Well...

12:41.360 --> 12:45.000
the reason no one outright says it...

12:45.000 --> 12:47.490
is that the moment of realization 
and the process of getting there...

12:47.490 --> 12:51.120
are very important to the people involved.

12:51.120 --> 12:53.490
Not allowing them to discover 
those things for themselves,

12:53.490 --> 12:57.280
trying to make them move forward, 
that's just our own ambitions taking hold.

12:57.600 --> 12:58.370
But...

12:58.740 --> 13:01.680
maybe this is something 
you can't understand yet?

13:02.560 --> 13:04.000
I understand.

13:04.000 --> 13:07.680
You're telling me to be considerate 
of their feelings, right?

13:07.680 --> 13:09.180
You're so sharp!

13:09.680 --> 13:12.930
Please don't treat me like a child.

13:13.320 --> 13:16.180
Why'd you say something like that?

13:16.180 --> 13:18.100
Did you lose control of yourself?

13:18.100 --> 13:21.740
Well, I couldn't think of anything else.

13:21.740 --> 13:24.180
Still, of all things.

13:24.180 --> 13:27.570
You and Giselbert don't do 
that very often, do you?

13:27.570 --> 13:29.570
Why would I do that with him?

13:33.280 --> 13:35.150
It's starting to come down.

13:40.460 --> 13:45.590
Oh, aren't you happy? This is lovely.

13:50.010 --> 13:53.080
Things are lively today, 
aren't they, Frederica?

13:53.790 --> 13:56.360
I hope that lady saint will find happiness.

13:56.800 --> 13:58.860
Please watch over her, won't you?

14:07.050 --> 14:10.450
Lawren, where are we going?

14:10.450 --> 14:12.120
It's just a little farther.

14:17.330 --> 14:19.160
It's should happen soon.

14:31.410 --> 14:34.010
It's beautiful, Lawren!

14:34.520 --> 14:37.010
It's so beautiful!

14:41.000 --> 14:43.140
Lady Saint,

14:43.140 --> 14:46.210
would it be all right for me to think 
that you consider me like family, too?

14:46.210 --> 14:48.900
Wh-What is this all of a sudden?!

14:48.900 --> 14:50.120
Of course!

14:50.120 --> 14:53.230
You could say we're family 
or that I'd like to become part of your family!

14:53.230 --> 14:56.150
The other day, you said 
that the people you eat with,

14:56.150 --> 14:58.250
the people you say "good night" to,

14:58.250 --> 15:02.920
and the people you say "hello" to in
 the morning are your family, so I thought...

15:02.920 --> 15:06.420
Oh, you meant it that way.

15:06.790 --> 15:08.760
Yes.

15:09.240 --> 15:13.520
I do think of you like family, Lawren.

15:20.020 --> 15:21.890
L-L-Lawren?!

15:21.890 --> 15:25.030
If you're family, then you 
should do things like this.

15:25.030 --> 15:27.400
That's what Miss Hazelita told me.

15:27.400 --> 15:31.320
<b>In chaos</b>

15:27.410 --> 15:31.320
I-If you're family, then, yes, 
you might do things like this.

15:31.780 --> 15:33.230
I'm sorry.

15:33.230 --> 15:35.040
I've made you uncomfortable, haven't I?

15:35.040 --> 15:36.110
What?

15:36.110 --> 15:37.400
Y-You haven't made me uncomfortable!

15:37.400 --> 15:38.850
Really? But...

15:38.850 --> 15:39.960
Actually...

15:39.960 --> 15:43.310
You've made me hap...

15:44.450 --> 15:46.080
I'm so sorry!

15:46.080 --> 15:47.150
I won't do it again!

15:47.150 --> 15:48.650
I won't have that!

15:48.650 --> 15:49.580
What?

15:49.580 --> 15:53.470
I-It isn't that I don't like it.

15:53.470 --> 15:55.720
So, um...

15:57.510 --> 16:00.100
If you'd do it again...

16:02.150 --> 16:04.970
You're much too straightforward.

16:10.590 --> 16:12.110
Lawren...

16:12.110 --> 16:17.280
it seems as though you're fumbling around, 
trying out ways of acting like a family.

16:17.750 --> 16:22.120
You say that you think of me as family, 
but you seem anxious.

16:22.630 --> 16:28.030
Lawren, is there something in particular 
you're seeking to find in a family?

16:30.300 --> 16:32.260
Lawrence,

16:32.260 --> 16:35.880
death isn't something to be feared.

16:35.880 --> 16:39.800
Leaving on a journey 
is something to be happy about.

16:39.800 --> 16:44.140
But if there were 
anything I might regret...

16:44.140 --> 16:50.840
it would be leaving you here, 
all alone, in this big house.

16:52.680 --> 16:57.010
Since my grandfather passed 
away, I've been alone.

16:57.640 --> 17:01.940
But since that day, the day
you appeared, Lady Saint...

17:03.450 --> 17:09.200
I've lived with you... 
and I've been so happy every day.

17:09.520 --> 17:13.600
I thought that if we were family, 
then you might always stay by my side.

17:14.160 --> 17:16.630
I found I couldn't help thinking about it.

17:19.970 --> 17:21.520
I'm here.

17:23.100 --> 17:25.070
I'll always be here with you.

17:25.890 --> 17:28.020
Because we're family!

17:40.650 --> 17:42.460
L-Lawren?

17:42.460 --> 17:44.530
I-I'm sorry.

17:44.840 --> 17:49.620
Um, I just had this sudden, 
overwhelming urge to run away.

17:52.640 --> 17:54.000
Lady Saint?!

17:54.000 --> 17:55.560
Lawren,

17:55.560 --> 17:59.000
I don't think you know how 
to ask your family to hold you...

17:59.000 --> 18:01.880
so I'm showing you how it's done.

18:05.640 --> 18:09.230
Now, you're not allowed to 
forget this, all right?

18:09.740 --> 18:11.080
I won't.

18:18.760 --> 18:19.860
Ow!

18:21.120 --> 18:24.200
I heard a loud noise! Are you all right?

18:24.200 --> 18:26.610
Good morning, Lawren.

18:26.610 --> 18:30.190
I was still half-asleep 
and ran into the wall.

18:30.190 --> 18:31.880
Good morning.

18:31.880 --> 18:34.050
How half-asleep are you?

18:34.050 --> 18:36.150
I thought the wall was you, Lawren.

18:36.150 --> 18:38.800
Really, how asleep are you?

18:38.800 --> 18:40.290
Lawren?

18:40.290 --> 18:41.780
Were you in the middle of cooking?

18:43.330 --> 18:45.300
I guess I brought it with me.

18:45.300 --> 18:46.940
I-I'm sorry!

18:46.940 --> 18:48.690
I've made a nuisance of myself, haven't I?

18:48.690 --> 18:51.600
It's only natural for me to come running 
when something happens.

18:51.600 --> 18:53.360
Because we're family!

18:55.080 --> 18:56.860
Family...

19:01.120 --> 19:02.700
In spite of what you say,

19:02.700 --> 19:05.410
we end up eating three meals 
a day here, don't we?

19:05.410 --> 19:08.760
That's because I've decided 
to take them at their word.

19:08.760 --> 19:10.660
Oh, she's gone all defiant.

19:10.660 --> 19:13.840
I'd prefer it if you lived 
with us the way you did before!

19:13.840 --> 19:14.920
What do you think?

19:14.920 --> 19:16.610
That would be nice.

19:16.610 --> 19:18.290
What are you talking about?

19:18.290 --> 19:20.290
We absolutely cannot do that.

19:20.290 --> 19:21.430
You heard her.

19:21.430 --> 19:23.160
I see.

19:23.160 --> 19:26.070
But we can see them every day like this.

19:26.070 --> 19:27.860
That's true!

19:27.860 --> 19:28.850
Say...

19:29.560 --> 19:32.440
isn't this egg sort of burnt?

19:32.440 --> 19:34.490
That's unusual.

19:34.490 --> 19:36.980
To think Lawrence would make 
a mistake like that.

19:37.910 --> 19:40.560
That's my fault!

19:40.560 --> 19:41.360
What?

19:41.360 --> 19:43.620
It isn't your fault, Lady Saint.

19:43.620 --> 19:45.730
I wasn't paying proper attention.

19:45.730 --> 19:48.080
No, it is my fault.

19:48.080 --> 19:48.880
No, it isn't.

19:48.880 --> 19:51.700
It's my fault for not turning off the heat.

19:51.700 --> 19:54.940
No, it's because I was half-asleep 
and ran into the wall.

19:54.940 --> 19:57.960
No, it isn't your fault, Lady Saint.

19:57.960 --> 20:01.230
It isn't your fault either, Lawren!

20:01.230 --> 20:03.090
Lady saints can't lie!

20:03.090 --> 20:05.640
It isn't about lying, it's...

20:05.640 --> 20:07.870
Come on. Hurry up and eat!

20:07.870 --> 20:09.520
Yes.

20:09.520 --> 20:13.110
Honestly. They get along 
so well, don't they?

21:46.310 --> 21:48.100
<i>I'm Lily!</i>

21:48.100 --> 21:50.860
<i>I always visit the church to play!</i>

21:51.500 --> 21:55.410
<i>Before, when I said that 
I was going to marry the pastor...</i>

21:55.410 --> 21:58.500
<i>the lady saint made a weird face.</i>

21:58.500 --> 22:02.000
<i>She told me all sorts of things 
about the pastor,</i>

22:02.000 --> 22:05.000
<i>but I didn't really 
understand what she was saying.</i>

22:05.480 --> 22:06.760
<i>But, you know what?</i>

22:07.670 --> 22:10.260
Pastor! Good morning!

22:10.260 --> 22:12.430
Good morning, Lily!

22:12.430 --> 22:15.350
Did you bring flowers for us again today?

22:15.350 --> 22:16.240
I did!

22:16.240 --> 22:18.760
I'm gonna give them to the lady saint later!

22:18.760 --> 22:19.510
Oh!

22:19.510 --> 22:22.260
The space next to 
the lady saint is free now!

22:22.260 --> 22:23.880
I'm going to go now.

22:26.030 --> 22:27.700
Lady Saint!

22:27.700 --> 22:29.280
Lily!

22:30.060 --> 22:32.880
<i>The lady saint is always 
beautiful and sparkly.</i>

22:32.880 --> 22:35.280
<i>She's amazing.</i>

22:35.640 --> 22:37.420
The weather is nice today, isn't it?

22:37.420 --> 22:39.020
Yes, it is!

22:39.020 --> 22:42.260
I'm glad you didn't get 
drenched by rain, Lily.

22:42.260 --> 22:45.460
You seem like you'd come here 
even on rainy days.

22:45.460 --> 22:47.440
What? You mean I can't?

22:47.440 --> 22:48.920
Lady Saint?

22:49.310 --> 22:51.370
I'm sorry, Lily. I'll just be a moment.

22:51.370 --> 22:52.920
What is it?

22:52.920 --> 22:54.810
<i>I know, you know?</i>

22:54.810 --> 22:58.810
<i>When the lady saint 
is close to the pastor...</i>

22:58.810 --> 23:01.360
<i>she gets really cute!</i>

23:02.070 --> 23:04.320
Then, perhaps we'll see you again next week.

23:04.320 --> 23:06.610
Yes, we'll be waiting.

23:07.560 --> 23:09.610
Here, for you! Flowers!

23:09.870 --> 23:12.120
You're giving them both to me?

23:12.120 --> 23:14.680
Yes! And also...

23:17.510 --> 23:21.090
I'll let you have the pastor, Lady Saint.

23:22.380 --> 23:24.100
Bye-bye!
